--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components and data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This work builds on Google Research's Perch and perch-hoplite:
    https://github.com/google-research/perch-hoplite
Perch V2 is distributed under its own license terms. The classifiers
released here are linear probes trained on top of frozen Perch V2
embeddings; they contain no Perch V2 model parameters.

Portions of the pipeline code derive from or interoperate with
perch-hoplite (Apache License 2.0, Copyright Google LLC).

The raw MARS hydrophone recordings underlying this work are published
independently as part of the Pacific Ocean Sound archive on the AWS
Open Data registry, under their own terms. They are neither re-hosted
nor relicensed here. See data_access/how_to_get_raw_audio.md.

Visual ground truth for killer whale presence is drawn from published
encounter reports of the California Killer Whale Project, cited as
reference material and not redistributed.

The MARS cabled observatory is operated by the Monterey Bay Aquarium
Research Institute.
